Vacaturebeschrijving
   Wolfram Chain is looking for a motivated Class C truck driver for a transport company that supplies catering and hospitality businesses, based in Berkel en Rodenrijs.You will work closely with a direct colleague, get to know many regular customers, and at the end of the day, you can enjoy a hot meal at the office for a small fee.Ready for a new challenge? Check out this vacancy or get in touch with us!  Functieomschrijving:
 What you will do:As a Class C truck driver for this company, your working days will be focused on supplying hospitality businesses. Your responsibilities include:- Representing the company and having a friendly conversation with customers;
- Working from Monday to Friday;
- You will deliver food and drinks;
- Want to work extra hours? That's possible. Prefer to work four days a week? That's possible too.


  Functievereisten:
 What we expect from you as a driver:- You have a valid Class C or CE driving licence;
- You are physically fit and comfortable performing physically demanding tasks;
- You have a good command of either Dutch or English.


  Arbeidsvoorwaarden:
 What you can expect in return:- A gross monthly salary between €3,000 and €5,000;
- Overtime paid at 130%, plus an ADV allowance;
- A good pension scheme in accordance with the collective labour agreement (CAO);
- 24 paid vacation days;
- The opportunity to follow internal training courses;
- Getting your class CE license for free;
- A fresh, hot meal every day at the office for just €2.50;
- A permanent contract upon good performance.

Interested?Apply now! 
Salarisomschrijving€3000 - €5000 monthly

Are you a natural leader who knows how to motivate a team and keep logistics operations running smoothly? For our client in Eemshaven, we are looking for a High Tech Team Leader. In this role, you will lead a team in a fast-paced, international high-tech environment where safety, quality, and efficiency are key.

What will you do?
As a High Tech Team Leader, you are responsible for the daily management of your team and the performance of the logistics operation. You make sure everyone knows what needs to be done, processes run according to plan, and safety and quality standards are met.

Your responsibilities include:

- Managing, coaching, and motivating your team within a high-tech logistics environment;
- Coordinating and monitoring daily logistics processes according to strict safety, quality, and data center procedures;
- Monitoring KPIs such as productivity, quality, SLAs, and 5S;
- Identifying bottlenecks and taking action when necessary;
- Initiating and supporting process improvements together with the supervisor and other departments;
- Creating a safe, structured, and positive working environment for your team.

We are looking for someone who feels comfortable taking responsibility and leading people in a dynamic environment.

You bring:

- Proven experience as a Team Leader, Supervisor, or Coordinator within logistics or production;
- Strong organizational skills and natural leadership qualities;
- The ability to coach, motivate, and develop a team;
- Affinity with high-tech, hardware, and working according to fixed procedures and guidelines;
- A proactive mindset and the confidence to identify and implement improvements;
- A good command of the English language;
- Dutch language skills are a plus.

You are someone who takes initiative, is not afraid to make decisions, and wants to grow together with the organization.
